WEBVTT

1
00:00:07.667 --> 00:00:11.260
Columbus took Mandy to his cabin.

2
00:00:11.261 --> 00:00:14.926
"You will be safe here," he said.

3
00:00:14.927 --> 00:00:19.563
Curious, Mandy picked up a round metal object.

4
00:00:19.564 --> 00:00:24.039
Its pointy, moving hands were like a clock's.

5
00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:27.974
"What's this?" asked Mandy.

6
00:00:27.975 --> 00:00:31.846
"It's an astrolabe," explained Columbus.

7
00:00:31.847 --> 00:00:35.314
"It measures the height of the sun from the horizon.

8
00:00:35.315 --> 00:00:38.995
It helps us know where we are on the ocean."

9
00:00:38.996 --> 00:00:42.262
Columbus took the astrolabe and said,

10
00:00:42.263 --> 00:00:47.689
"I have to go now. Stay here."

11
00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:51.397
Meanwhile, Vinnie was getting hungry.

12
00:00:51.398 --> 00:00:55.048
A sailor's life wasn't much fun.

13
00:00:55.049 --> 00:01:00.276
"We're all going to starve," said an old sailor nearby.

14
00:01:00.277 --> 00:01:05.806
"Monsters will eat us before we starve!" screamed another.

15
00:01:05.807 --> 00:01:09.877
"I want to go home!" thought Vinnie.

16
00:01:09.878 --> 00:01:13.472
Manuel was tying a knot in a rope.

17
00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:19.863
Another boy was standing by a large coil of rope, holding an hourglass.

18
00:01:19.864 --> 00:01:24.294
When the sand emptied into the bottom, the boy cried:

19
00:01:24.295 --> 00:01:26.423
"One glass is gone.

20
00:01:26.424 --> 00:01:28.785
Now the second begins!"

21
00:01:28.786 --> 00:01:32.808
"What's he doing?" Vinnie asked Manuel.

22
00:01:32.809 --> 00:01:36.206
"We take turns turning over the hourglass.

23
00:01:36.207 --> 00:01:42.033
Each time it empties, a half hour has gone by," explained Manuel.

24
00:01:42.034 --> 00:01:47.510
"After eight turns, or four hours, another boy takes over."

25
00:01:47.511 --> 00:01:49.807
The boy called to Vinnie,

26
00:01:49.808 --> 00:01:52.426
"Hey, take over a minute, will you?"

27
00:01:52.427 --> 00:01:56.008
He put the hourglass into Vinnie's hands.

28
00:01:56.009 --> 00:02:00.111
"It's the second half of the hour," said the boy.

29
00:02:00.112 --> 00:02:03.882
He ran off before Vinnie could protest.

30
00:02:03.883 --> 00:02:06.552
"Here," said Manuel.

31
00:02:06.553 --> 00:02:11.018
He took a biscuit out of his pocket and gave it to Vinnie.

32
00:02:11.019 --> 00:02:16.760
Biscuits were used to mark the time after each turn of the hourglass.

33
00:02:16.761 --> 00:02:20.277
Vinnie thought he was supposed to eat it.

34
00:02:20.278 --> 00:02:24.484
"Ow!" cried Vinnie, after he tried to bite it.

35
00:02:24.485 --> 00:02:29.481
The biscuit was so hard that Vinnie put it down on the ropes.

36
00:02:29.482 --> 00:02:34.104
Meanwhile, Mandy sat alone in the captain's cabin.

37
00:02:34.105 --> 00:02:38.023
The cabin boy had left her a biscuit to eat.

38
00:02:38.024 --> 00:02:40.389
She put it in her pocket.

39
00:02:40.390 --> 00:02:44.259
Suddenly, there was a loud boom.

40
00:02:44.260 --> 00:02:47.743
Mandy, ran out onto the deck.

41
00:02:47.744 --> 00:02:51.457
"What was that?" she shouted.

42
00:02:51.458 --> 00:02:54.977
"It's the Pinta!" cried someone.

43
00:02:54.978 --> 00:02:57.285
"The ship needs help!"

44
00:02:57.286 --> 00:03:01.826
At that moment, she heard a familiar voice shouting,

45
00:03:01.827 --> 00:03:06.522
"One glass is gone, and now the second begins!"

46
00:03:06.523 --> 00:03:10.323
"Vinnie!" she cried happily.

47
00:03:10.324 --> 00:03:13.951
"Mandy! Am I glad to see you!"

48
00:03:13.952 --> 00:03:16.773
he exclaimed when she ran up.

49
00:03:16.774 --> 00:03:20.549
He put the hourglass on top of the ropes.

50
00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:24.308
"What are you doing?" she asked.

51
00:03:24.309 --> 00:03:29.304
"Every thirty minutes, I turn this hourglass over.

52
00:03:29.305 --> 00:03:33.542
Each time, Manuel brings a biscuit.

53
00:03:33.543 --> 00:03:38.003
They're so hard I can't eat them," said Vinnie.

54
00:03:38.004 --> 00:03:39.929
"Don't eat them!"

55
00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:43.798
Mandy shouted, pulling out the photo.

56
00:03:43.799 --> 00:03:47.104
"We need them! See?"

57
00:03:47.105 --> 00:03:49.885
The photo was glowing blue.

58
00:03:49.886 --> 00:03:54.520
"But there are only two biscuits!" cried Vinnie.

59
00:03:54.521 --> 00:03:57.206
"We need three to go home."

60
00:03:57.207 --> 00:04:03.430
"Don't worry," said Mandy, pulling the biscuit from her pocket.

61
00:04:03.431 --> 00:04:07.541
Mandy placed it next to the other biscuits.

62
00:04:07.542 --> 00:04:12.159
In the photo, the hourglass glowed red.

63
00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:16.670
"I'm so glad we're leaving!" cried Vinnie.

64
00:04:16.671 --> 00:04:24.991
The children closed their eyes and fell down the dark tunnel.
